# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `service-go` Copier template at `ika100/sdlc-foundry`. The template encodes the platform's Go conventions (platform ADR-010):

- Go {{ go_version }} via devbox; module `{{ module_name }}`
- `chi` router, stdlib `log/slog` JSON logging
- `golangci-lint` (curated `.golangci.yml`) + `go build` as the quality gate; `govulncheck` for dependency audit
- `go test -race -cover` (stdlib `testing`)
- Static binary in `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` → `{{ docker_registry }}/{{ project_name }}`; version injected via ldflags from the git tag
- No Kubernetes manifests here: the system's gitops-app repo owns them (platform ADR-017); this repo ships a container image
- GitHub topic `deployable-service` for ArgoCD discovery
- Claude Code agents from the `sdlc-foundry` marketplace (`svc-go` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, Dockerfile, Go bump, lint config) arrive through `copier update`; `cmd/`, `internal/`, `go.mod`, `go.sum` and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
